# the effects' one pool (dsp/efx.h, 78 blocks of 2 KB): a new project's sends (FX I's delay, 24 blocks; FX II on lush,
# 26: a new project's is lush S, 11, since 2026-11-27, so set here) leave room for a track's delay (24) beside them; a second track's delay finds none ("no memory": it passes dry).
# (The sends each their own blocks: FX II placed beside FX I, not over it, engine.c pool_sends; over it, the tracks
# had 26 blocks more, and the second delay found room). Whoever holds memory keeps it: Master FX's delay (24) finds
# none beside the sends and the track's delay ("not playing: memory full"), its tape a block
# (2026-11-27: a delay takes what its time needs at the tempo, efx_delay_blocks; at 60 BPM a default delay
# needs its longest line, 24 blocks, as these counts assume)
bpm 60
knob 12 s1x1 lush
wait 300
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
expect room1.1 1
knob 1 ctype 16
knob 1 cmix 100
wait 100
expect par1.ctype 16
expect room1.1 1
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
knob 2 ctype 16
knob 2 cmix 100
wait 100
expect room2.1 0
expect room1.1 1
# the first track's delay off: its blocks go to the second's
knob 1 ctype 0
wait 100
expect room2.1 1
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
# Master FX's delay at its longest (24): none (the second track's delay keeps its blocks); its tape's wow a block, beside
# them
mst color delay
mst camount 127
mst cmix 64
wait 100
expect mstroom 0
expect room2.1 1
expect fxroom1 1
expect fxroom2 1
mst color tape
wait 100
expect mstroom 1
expect room2.1 1
mst color off
wait 100
expect mstroom 1
expect room2.1 1
